## 2. Inspection (cite path:line for every finding)

- [ ] Names state meaning and unit; no abbreviations a newcomer must guess.
- [ ] Numeric literals other than 0 and 1 are named constants.
- [ ] Public functions, classes and modules have docstrings with arguments,
      returns and raised errors.
- [ ] Types are concrete; no `Any`, casts or untyped public signatures.
- [ ] Code sits in the owning layer; dependencies point inward; I/O at edges.
- [ ] Errors are specific, chained and actionable; nothing is swallowed.
- [ ] Failure paths and boundary values have tests, not only the happy path.
- [ ] Documentation, examples and changelog match the new behavior.
- [ ] No secrets, personal data, absolute local paths or debug leftovers.
- [ ] No generated file was edited by hand.

